# CI-only Bazel settings. Loaded explicitly by the CI workflow
# (`bazel --bazelrc=.bazelrc.ci ...`); it is NOT auto-imported, so a local
# `bazel test //...` still runs every target.
#
# Two exclusions, for different reasons.
#
# `local_only` — needs the composite-capable dev frxlib. Vmapping a hash-frx
# composite marker takes the CompositeOp op plus its batching rule, and CI runs
# the published wheel, which has neither. Run them locally against that dev
# frxlib. Drop this filter (and the tags) once the published frx pin carries the
# composite backport.
#
# `slow_kat` — the exhaustive known-answer sweeps: every parameter set of a
# scheme against every published vector. They are the standards-exactness gate,
# so they must run, but a full sweep per PR makes review painful. The scheduled
# CI run puts them back (see .github/workflows/ci.yml); tag a suite `slow_kat`
# only when it is genuinely a sweep, since a tag here is a suite that does not
# gate a merge.
test --test_tag_filters=-local_only,-slow_kat
